nal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schlotterer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><year>1994</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>513</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8015444</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Nues</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>1995</year><volume>250</volume><fpage>24</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7602595</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Joseph</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>1999</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>4533</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10556307</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Proposed secondary structure of ITS2 regions of Group 1/Clade 1 (A1) and Group 2/Clade 2 (A2). Multiple alignment of the ITS2 sequences of <italic>An. culicifacies</italic>, derived from the retrieved and improved GenBank sequences using secondary structure analyses. Seq1 (SLB, SLE, Camb2, Camb3, Camb4, Camb5, ChUn2 and India E) and Seq2 (Iran A2, IranA3, Iran A4 and Camb A) (b), Table 1 (see <xref ref-type="supplementary-material" rid="SD1">supplementary material</xref>)). Phylogenetic tree of <italic>An. Culicifacies</italic> species based on the sequences of the ITS2 of rDNA cistron. Numerical numbers at the nodes are bootstrap values. The lengths of the horizontal lines are proportional to the minimum number of nucleotide differences required to join nodes. Numerical numbers at horizontal lines are node lengths (c).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="97320630002456F1"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>